getpath: take the home from the slicc command's own argv, never from a
variable a caller can set, and under -E/-I take nothing else from the
environment or the cwd either (homescoop#1572, #1504, #1144); venv: always
symlink the interpreter on wasi (homescoop#1269).

The slicc command runs python as /usr/bin/python3 (a registered copy) with
PYTHONHOME set to the package and its argv prefixed by
"-X slicc_home=<package>/" (package.json args). A caller's environment
overrides the command's env, but not its argv prefix, so getpath takes
the home from orig_argv[1:3] when PYTHONHOME is not used: always under
-I/-E, which ignore PYTHONHOME as stock CPython does. That home counts as
set by the embedder (home_was_set), so no ._pth file replaces it.
Under -I/-E getpath also ignores PATH, PYTHONEXECUTABLE and
__PYVENV_LAUNCHER__, takes the executable only from an absolute argv[0]
(slicc-kernel's argv0Path, how a venv's bin/python starts), never from a
cwd-relative one, and without an executable looks for pyvenv.cfg only in
the home's bin/ and the home, never in the cwd. slicc starts a
#!/usr/bin/python3 -I script with argv[0] "python3", so a caller's PATH or
cwd could otherwise pick a pyvenv.cfg and run its site-packages' .pth.
A venv's copied bin/python runs as a bare wasm, without the command's env
and with argv[0] reduced to its name, so it finds neither PYTHONHOME nor
pyvenv.cfg; a symlink resolves to the registered command.

--- a/Lib/venv/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/venv/__init__.py
@@ -52,6 +52,13 @@
         self.system_site_packages = system_site_packages
         self.clear = clear
         self.symlinks = symlinks
+        # homescoop wasix-python (homescoop#1269): a copied interpreter can't
+        # run. The kernel starts a bare copy of python.wasm without the slicc
+        # command's environment and with argv[0] reduced to its name, so it
+        # can find neither PYTHONHOME nor its pyvenv.cfg. A symlink resolves to
+        # the registered /usr/bin/python3 and works: always link.
+        if sys.platform == 'wasi' and not symlinks:
+            self.symlinks = True
         self.upgrade = upgrade
         self.with_pip = with_pip
         self.orig_prompt = prompt
